      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "El tercer día, Set no esperó su turno.",
          "en": "On the third day, Set did not wait his turn."
        },
        {
          "es": "Se abrió paso por el costado de su madre y nació antes de tiempo.",
          "en": "He tore his way out through his mother's side and was born before his time."
        },
        {
          "es": "Tenía la piel pálida, el pelo rojo como el desierto y la fuerza de una tormenta.",
          "en": "He had pale skin, red hair like the desert, and the strength of a storm."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los egipcios lo adoraban y le temían. Era el señor del desierto, del trueno y de las tormentas de arena.",
          "en": "The Egyptians worshipped and feared him. He was lord of the desert, thunder and sandstorms."
        },
        {
          "es": "Más tarde, Ra puso a Set en la proa de su barca para defenderla durante la noche.",
          "en": "Later, Ra put Set at the front of his boat to defend it at night."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los egipcios creían que esos cinco días eran peligrosos, y el de Set, el tercero, el peor.",
          "en": "The Egyptians thought the five days were dangerous, and Set's day was the worst."
        }
      ],
